      "message": "Might be easier to read as `stmt-\u003eis\u003cContinueStatement\u003e() || stmt-\u003eis\u003cBreakStatement\u003e()`? NBD though.\n\nAlso, ideally, we would detect this as unreachable code and eliminate it in the front end DCE pass. This is where it should happen: \nhttps://osscs.corp.google.com/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/sksl/transform/SkSLEliminateUnreachableCode.cpp;l\u003d124;drc\u003d8ccbeeebc34d80ac9525dfcca122d196bbbb0630\n\nWe no longer support `continue` escaping out of a switch (because D3D9 doesn\u0027t!) so it should be pretty easy to handle. Before that change it was a bit hairy.\n\nIt\u0027s totally fine to land this and fix the problem now, to unblock the roller. The front-end fix would just be nice polish (and will make the output from the other backends slightly cleaner).",
