      "writtenOn": "2022-07-02T20:11:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think `fCurrentBlock` is zero when we are emitting code that comes immediately after a branch (rendering it unreachable). In these cases, we insert a dummy label so that the validator won\u0027t complain:\n\nhttps://osscs.corp.google.com/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/sksl/codegen/SkSLSPIRVCodeGenerator.cpp;l\u003d408-410;drc\u003d8ccbeeebc34d80ac9525dfcca122d196bbbb0630\n\nThis can happen if the DCE pass fails to eliminate something unreachable. (This is very possible, especially considering DCE currently ignores switches entirely!)",
